1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,067
The H.U.N.T.E.R.: a machine sent back through time with one name in its memory.

2
00:00:04,067 --> 00:00:04,353
Yours.

3
00:00:04,573 --> 00:00:05,853
Here's how it plays.

4
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:09,874
Put the two Countdown tokens on the back of the Finale card.

5
00:00:09,874 --> 00:00:14,203
Then pick three Cybernetic Part tokens at random and, without looking, stack them

6
00:00:14,203 --> 00:00:16,395
face down on top. That's a stack of five.

7
00:00:16,615 --> 00:00:19,724
Build the Terror deck as normal without the Hunter Mark X card.

8
00:00:19,724 --> 00:00:23,722
Then shuffle the Mark X card with the bottom two cards of the deck, and put those

9
00:00:23,722 --> 00:00:24,956
three back on the bottom.

10
00:00:25,176 --> 00:00:29,229
The red Core box Killer meeple is the Mark V, on the Killer start space.

11
00:00:29,229 --> 00:00:33,957
Keep the silver Mark X meeple, the Mark V Ally card and four Action cubes beside you

12
00:00:33,957 --> 00:00:34,520
for later.

13
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:38,447
The Hunter comes in two models. You start against the Mark V.

14
00:00:38,447 --> 00:00:42,224
Near the end of the game the Mark X arrives and becomes the Active Killer.

15
00:00:42,444 --> 00:00:45,879
Any rule or card that says the Hunter means whichever model is active.

16
00:00:46,099 --> 00:00:50,319
The health markers and Final Health token on the Killer board belong to the Mark X.

17
00:00:50,319 --> 00:00:52,200
The Mark V is beaten a different way.

18
00:00:53,033 --> 00:00:55,084
The Hunter doesn't care about bystanders.

19
00:00:55,084 --> 00:00:57,535
Bloodlust does not go up when a Victim is killed.

20
00:00:57,755 --> 00:01:02,081
Instead, Bloodlust goes up when the Hunter damages you or an Ally, or when it takes

21
00:01:02,081 --> 00:01:02,811
damage itself.

22
00:01:03,031 --> 00:01:07,211
But only once per phase. If you play Retaliate and you both hurt each other, it's

23
00:01:07,211 --> 00:01:08,449
still just one increase.

24
00:01:08,669 --> 00:01:13,050
In the Panic phase, as well as the normal panic rules, Victims in the Hunter's space

25
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:15,240
also panic if Bloodlust went up that turn.

26
00:01:16,067 --> 00:01:20,589
To beat the Mark V you destroy its Cybernetic Parts, the face-down tokens on the

27
00:01:20,589 --> 00:01:22,851
Finale card. Each Part takes two damage.

28
00:01:23,071 --> 00:01:26,617
Damage from several attacks adds up, but only within the same phase.

29
00:01:26,617 --> 00:01:30,684
For example, a Weak Attack for one damage, then a Furious Strike for one more,

30
00:01:30,684 --> 00:01:31,519
destroys a Part.

31
00:01:31,739 --> 00:01:35,671
If you'd stopped after the Weak Attack, that single damage would be wasted when the

32
00:01:35,671 --> 00:01:36,240
phase ended.

33
00:01:36,460 --> 00:01:40,843
Big turns pay: five damage in one phase destroys two Parts, and the fifth point is

34
00:01:40,843 --> 00:01:41,111
lost.

35
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:46,415
Each time a Part is destroyed, take the top Part token off the Finale card, roll a

36
00:01:46,415 --> 00:01:50,623
die, and place the token in the Mark V's space or next to it, using the Panic

37
00:01:50,623 --> 00:01:53,411
numbers on its space, just like panicking a Victim.

38
00:01:53,631 --> 00:01:56,651
When the last Part token is gone, the Mark V shuts down.

39
00:01:56,651 --> 00:02:01,129
Leave its meeple where it is. Take its Dark Power card, revealing it if needed, and

40
00:02:01,129 --> 00:02:04,959
slide it under the Mark V Ally card so the ability shows at the bottom.

41
00:02:05,179 --> 00:02:08,409
If that happened in your Action phase, carry on with your turn.

42
00:02:08,409 --> 00:02:10,615
In any other phase, the phase ends at once.

43
00:02:10,615 --> 00:02:13,179
From now on the Mark V isn't a Killer or an Enemy.

44
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,235
Once only the two Countdown tokens are left on the Finale card, ignore the Killer

45
00:02:18,235 --> 00:02:21,424
action on the back of the Finale and don't draw Terror cards.

46
00:02:21,644 --> 00:02:25,814
Instead, at the start of each Killer phase, remove one Countdown token and raise

47
00:02:25,814 --> 00:02:26,700
Bloodlust by one.

48
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:31,052
When the second token comes off, draw a new Setup card and put the silver Mark X

49
00:02:31,052 --> 00:02:35,339
meeple on its Killer start space. The Mark X is now the Active Killer, and resolves

50
00:02:35,339 --> 00:02:37,715
the Killer phase as normal from the next turn.

51
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:42,368
If you're slow, the Hunter Mark X Terror card, hidden near the bottom of the deck,

52
00:02:42,368 --> 00:02:43,163
forces the issue.

53
00:02:43,383 --> 00:02:47,997
If the Mark V is still active, it shuts down immediately and Bloodlust jumps to the

54
00:02:47,997 --> 00:02:52,667
top of the track. Any remaining Part tokens are dropped in its space, and the Mark X

55
00:02:52,667 --> 00:02:54,391
inherits any Minor Dark Powers.

56
00:02:54,611 --> 00:02:59,187
If the Mark X isn't on the board yet, discard the Countdown tokens, draw a new Setup

57
00:02:59,187 --> 00:03:01,693
card and place the Mark X on its Killer space.

58
00:03:01,913 --> 00:03:05,159
Then discard the rest of the Terror deck and reveal the Finale.

59
00:03:05,159 --> 00:03:07,993
Even if another card discards it, you still resolve it.

60
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:11,557
The Mark V can be repaired and turned into your Ally.

61
00:03:11,557 --> 00:03:13,429
First, collect the Parts it dropped.

62
00:03:13,649 --> 00:03:17,531
In the Action phase, while in a token's space, spend one Time to pick it up.

63
00:03:17,531 --> 00:03:20,903
One Time per token. You can't grab them while just moving through.

64
00:03:21,123 --> 00:03:25,310
Keep them face down in your Backpack. You can collect Parts even before the Mark V

65
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:25,923
is defeated.

66
00:03:26,733 --> 00:03:31,165
Once the Mark V is defeated and you're in its space, spend one Time to flip one Part

67
00:03:31,165 --> 00:03:35,544
token from your Backpack, and put that many Health markers on the Mark V Ally card.

68
00:03:35,764 --> 00:03:40,123
The first time you do this, put the Ally card and its four Action cubes in your play

69
00:03:40,123 --> 00:03:41,887
area. The Mark V is now your Ally.

70
00:03:42,107 --> 00:03:46,383
Spend one more Time per extra Part, now or on later turns, to add more health.

71
00:03:46,383 --> 00:03:50,988
But if the repaired Mark V ever loses all its health, it's destroyed permanently and

72
00:03:50,988 --> 00:03:52,304
can't be repaired again.

73
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:56,846
Allies follow a few rules. They aren't Victims, so they don't follow you.

74
00:03:56,846 --> 00:04:00,965
Unless a card says otherwise, they can't carry Items or save Victims, and Victims

75
00:04:00,965 --> 00:04:01,880
won't follow them.

76
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:05,909
When you and an Ally share a space and one of you is attacked, you choose who takes

77
00:04:05,909 --> 00:04:06,047
it.

78
00:04:06,267 --> 00:04:11,067
Enemies usually only target an Ally when resolving a Final Girl or Victim target and

79
00:04:11,067 --> 00:04:15,525
the Ally is the closest. Even then, Victims in the Ally's space are hit first.

80
00:04:16,333 --> 00:04:20,804
The Ally card shows its Actions. To use one in the Action phase, put an Action cube

81
00:04:20,804 --> 00:04:24,952
on the leftmost box of that row. A row that already has a cube can't be used.

82
00:04:25,172 --> 00:04:27,683
Every Upkeep, slide every cube one box right.

83
00:04:27,683 --> 00:04:30,696
When it slides off the end, that action is free again.

84
00:04:30,696 --> 00:04:33,151
Rows with more boxes take longer to recover.

85
00:04:33,371 --> 00:04:36,382
The Mark V can attack for two damage or move one space.

86
00:04:36,382 --> 00:04:40,818
Its blue Reaction, usable in any phase, reduces the damage from an attack by one,

87
00:04:40,818 --> 00:04:43,611
and the card shows it hitting back with one damage.

88
00:04:43,831 --> 00:04:47,756
Its Dark Power card, tucked underneath, gives it a permanent Mark V Power.

89
00:04:48,567 --> 00:04:52,619
Each Dark Power has a top half for the Killer and a side panel for the repaired

90
00:04:52,619 --> 00:04:52,876
Ally.

91
00:04:53,096 --> 00:04:57,428
Reinforced Endoskeleton: the Mark V ignores all effects that make it lose health,

92
00:04:57,428 --> 00:05:00,797
though damage still counts. As an Ally it keeps that toughness.

93
00:05:01,017 --> 00:05:05,075
Cybernetic Agility: the Mark V moves one extra space for each Movement.

94
00:05:05,075 --> 00:05:08,847
As an Ally, when it moves at least one space it may move one more.

95
00:05:09,067 --> 00:05:12,901
Titanium-Laced Bio Tissue: each Part needs three damage, not two.

96
00:05:12,901 --> 00:05:15,851
As an Ally, each repair restores one extra health.

97
00:05:16,071 --> 00:05:20,646
The Epic M134 Minigun Armament gives it an attack range of nought to one, and when

98
00:05:20,646 --> 00:05:23,659
it attacks at range one you can't play Reaction cards.

99
00:05:23,659 --> 00:05:26,951
As an Ally it does one extra damage at range nought to one.

100
00:05:27,767 --> 00:05:32,451
Move or Be Eliminated sends it after the closest Victim, killing one Victim in every

101
00:05:32,451 --> 00:05:35,796
space it passes through, including where it starts and ends.

102
00:05:35,796 --> 00:05:38,305
Then Horror rises for each kill, up to twice.

103
00:05:38,525 --> 00:05:41,576
Shock and Awe makes you roll one fewer die on Reaction cards.

104
00:05:41,796 --> 00:05:46,337
The Advanced AI Minor Dark Power adds two health and raises Bloodlust an extra time

105
00:05:46,337 --> 00:05:48,580
whenever the Hunter hurts you or an Ally.

106
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:52,515
All three Finales start the Killer phase by coming straight for you.

107
00:05:52,735 --> 00:05:55,814
Relentless Pursuit: when revealed, Bloodlust goes up six.

108
00:05:55,814 --> 00:06:00,244
Each Killer phase the Mark X recovers health, then targets you, moves and attacks.

109
00:06:00,464 --> 00:06:04,217
Adaptive A.I.: Bloodlust plus one, then target you, move and attack.

110
00:06:04,217 --> 00:06:08,852
The Mark X does one extra damage, and damage from the Mark V is reduced by one, to a

111
00:06:08,852 --> 00:06:09,680
minimum of one.

112
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:14,111
Termination Mode... Active: Bloodlust plus one, then target you, move, and attack

113
00:06:14,111 --> 00:06:14,423
twice.

114
00:06:15,233 --> 00:06:19,587
A few tips. Damage doesn't carry between phases, so save your attacks for one big

115
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:22,060
turn and knock off Parts two damage at a time.

116
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:26,350
Collect the dropped Parts as you go, so you can rebuild the Mark V as a bodyguard

117
00:06:26,350 --> 00:06:27,656
before the Mark X arrives.

118
00:06:27,876 --> 00:06:31,641
Remember its Bloodlust comes from trading blows, not from Victims dying.

119
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:34,884
Players win about seventy per cent of logged games against it.

120
00:06:34,884 --> 00:06:35,407
Good luck.

